From a727e336ececda69e7f67efb0a9c3eee86b5fe77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cchavesd <CaioRodrigo.ChavesdosSantos@windriver.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 08:59:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Fix AppArmor profile template for container runtime
 compatibility

Add a signal rule to the crd2armor template so that container
runtimes (containerd/runc) can properly send SIGTERM/SIGKILL for
pod termination.

On AppArmor 4.x (Debian Trixie), signal permissions are not
implicitly granted even with the attach_disconnected flag. Without
an explicit signal rule, pods using SPO-generated AppArmor profiles
get stuck in Terminating state because runc cannot signal the
container init process.

Signed-off-by: cchavesd <CaioRodrigo.ChavesdosSantos@windriver.com>
---
 internal/pkg/daemon/apparmorprofile/crd2armor/crd2armor.go | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/internal/pkg/daemon/apparmorprofile/crd2armor/crd2armor.go b/internal/pkg/daemon/apparmorprofile/crd2armor/crd2armor.go
index e22f95d..c859fb9 100644
--- a/internal/pkg/daemon/apparmorprofile/crd2armor/crd2armor.go
+++ b/internal/pkg/daemon/apparmorprofile/crd2armor/crd2armor.go
@@ -81,6 +81,9 @@ profile {{.Name}} flags=({{.ProfileMode}},attach_disconnected,mediate_deleted) {
   umount,
   {{end}}
 
+  # Allow container runtime to signal processes for pod lifecycle management
+  signal,
+
   # Raw rules placeholder
 
   # Add default deny for known information leak/priv esc paths
-- 
2.54.0

